{
  "summary": "This first experiment established a baseline using an RNA-only, single-profile model with PCA (2000 components) and no image modality, aggregation, or fusion. The validation accuracy of ~48.5% (F1 ~46.4%) is an initial observation indicating that the raw PCA-reduced RNA signal alone yields modest predictive performance, though it is unclear whether this reflects the ceiling for RNA-only approaches or simply the floor before added complexity. It remains uncertain whether learned encoders, multiprofile aggregation, image modality, or cross-modal fusion could substantially improve beyond this baseline, and whether the task is broadly solvable at higher accuracy levels."
}

